From: ImmortalWrt Developer <developer@immortalwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: disable PPE flow offload when HNAT is enabled

When CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT or CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT_MODULE is
selected, mtk_probe() skips mtk_ppe_init() and mtk_eth_offload_init(),
so eth->flow_table is never initialized.

But mtk_eth_setup_tc() remains registered.  When nftables hardware
flow offload is enabled (e.g. firewall -> routing/NAT offload ->
hardware offload), nf_flow_table_offload_setup() calls:

    dev->netdev_ops->ndo_setup_tc(dev, TC_SETUP_FT, bo)

which registers the flow block cb.  The next flow offload work item then
calls mtk_flow_offload_replace(), which does:

    rhashtable_lookup(&eth->flow_table, &f->cookie, mtk_flow_ht_params)

with eth->flow_table.tbl == NULL, causing:

    Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual
    address 0000000000000008
    pc : mtk_flow_offload_replace+0x70/0x12e0

Return -EOPNOTSUPP from mtk_eth_setup_tc() when the MediaTek HNAT
driver is enabled so the mainline PPE flow offload path is not used.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
@@ -1042,6 +1042,9 @@
 int mtk_eth_setup_tc(struct net_device *dev, enum tc_setup_type type,
 		     void *type_data)
 {
+#if defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT) || defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT_MODULE)
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+#endif
 	switch (type) {
 	case TC_SETUP_BLOCK:
 	case TC_SETUP_FT:
